  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pair: ⟦{建|た}つ→建つ：12544_tatsu⟧ (intransitive, to be built). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{建|た}てる (build X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates completed state. {建|た}てている = 'is building' or 'has built.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{家|いえ}→家：00612_ie⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{建|た}てる (build a house)\n- ⟦ビル→ビル：01500_biru⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{建|た}てる (construct a building)\n- ⟦{建|た}て{替|か}える→建て替える：10541_tatekaeru⟧ (rebuild)\n- ⟦{一戸建|いっこだ}て→一戸建て：19687_ikkodate⟧ (detached house—noun)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {建|た}てる (transitive): (someone) builds X\n- ⟦{建|た}つ→建つ：12544_tatsu⟧ (intransitive): X is built/stands\n\nHOMOPHONE: Don't confuse with ⟦{立|た}てる→立てる：01196_tateru⟧ (to stand something up), which has the same reading but different meaning.\n- {建|た}てる ({建|た}): to build (structures)\n- ⟦{立|た}てる→立てる：01196_tateru⟧ ({立|た}): to stand up, erect (general)",
